<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept xml:lang="en-us" id="d2e106">
   <title>Button Bar</title>
   <conbody>
      <p>The bottom of the screen provides two sets of buttons for navigation and process control, and are the same for all four operation areas.  Click the arrow button on the far left to toggle between the two button sets.  Each button is identified with a letter and explained in the table below.</p>
      <p>
         <fig id="fig_yyt_n1g_vcc">
            <image href="media/image4.jpg" placement="break" id="image_zyt_n1g_vcc" align="center"/>
         </fig>
      </p>
      <table>
         <title>Button Descriptions</title>
         <tgroup cols="3">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="7.2%"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="17.1%"/>
            <colspec colname="c3" colwidth="69.3%"/>
            <thead>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Letter</p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Button Image</p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Function / Description</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>A</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image5.jpg" placement="break" id="image_hfz_xfg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Push these buttons to toggle to the other set of buttons</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>B</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image6.jpg" placement="break" id="image_exx_yfg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Password button used to log users on and off for process control</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>C</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image7.jpg" placement="break" id="image_oln_zfg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Opens the message system.  The acknowledgeable incoming alarm list is displayed in the working area.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>D</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image8.jpg" placement="break" id="image_rlg_1gg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Opens the "Reports" system dialog that provides the operator with an overview of all reports.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>E</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image9.jpg" placement="break" id="image_h4d_bgg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Opens the "Screen selection by name" system    dialog.  This function is used to select a graphic based   on a name, and to display it in the working area.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>F</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig id="fig_dqk_bgg_vcc">
                           <image href="media/image68.jpg" placement="break" id="image_rgb_zgg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>These buttons allow navigation between the screens for an operation area.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>G</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig id="fig_tdv_1hg_vcc">
                           <image href="media/image69.jpg" placement="break" id="image_hvs_2hg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Displays the process screen previously displayed in the working area. </p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>H</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image70.jpg" placement="break" id="image_osz_lhg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Store / Recall screens allow the operator to store and recall the process screen currently displayed in the working area.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>I </b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig id="fig_wmj_mhg_vcc">
                           <image href="media/image71.jpg" placement="break" id="image_lrt_phg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Recall / save / delete composition buttons allow the operator to manage different screen compositions. The combinations of screens and windows can be saved and recalled.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>J</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image29.jpg" id="image_kwc_rhg_vcc" placement="break"
                              class="- topic/image " align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Plant network - This screen gives the operator a quick overview of the    network configuration, and the current communication and health status of the plant equipment.  </p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>K</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image30.jpg" placement="break" id="image_b5t_rhg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Screen information function opens a dialog in the working area where information is shown for the currently displayed process picture.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>L</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image31.jpg" placement="break" id="image_vdr_shg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Acknowledge horn - The operator can acknowledge the failure horn. The alarm that triggered the horn is NOT acknowledged with this function.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>M</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image32.jpg" placement="break" id="image_pqk_thg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Acknowledge fault - The operator can acknowledge all the visible messages displayed in a process screen in the working areas</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>N</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image33.jpg" placement="break" id="image_wz3_5hg_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <u>Not Used</u>:  Language switch </p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>O</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig id="fig_akf_z1g_vcc">
                           <image href="media/image72.jpg" placement="break" id="image_fgw_h3g_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Lock / Unlock messages – This function is used to prevent the triggering of messages from all  affected measurement points through group  displays in the screen</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>P</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image38.jpg" placement="break" id="image_ch5_33g_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>User authorization function opens the User Administrator, which is used to specify permissions for individual users.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <p><b>Q</b></p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>
                        <fig>
                           <image href="media/image39.jpg" placement="break" id="image_ihk_j3g_vcc"
                              align="center"/>
                        </fig>
                     </p>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <p>Exit run time - This function allows the operator to exit the run time environment and enter the Windows environment.</p>
                  </entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table>
   </conbody>
</concept>
